==English==

===Etymology 1===
{{PIE root|en|bʰendʰ}}
{{unk|en}}; compare {{etyl|ang|en}} {{m|ang|bindele||a binding, a tying}},<ref name="OED1">“[http://dictionary.oed.com/cgi/entry/50022232 ˈbindle¹]” listed in the '''Oxford English Dictionary''' [2<sup>nd</sup> Ed.; 1989]</ref> and {{m|en|bundle}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun|?}}

# {{lb|en|now|_|Scots}}<ref name="OED1"/> Any given [[length]] of [[cord]], [[rope]], [[twine]], etc, used to [[bind]] something.<ref name="OED1"/>

===Etymology 2===
{{PIE root|en|bʰendʰ}}
[[File:Hobos2.jpg|thumb|The front [[hobo]] carries a '''bindle''' on the end of a stick.]]
[[File:Flavcocaine.jpg|thumb|Several '''bindles''' of [[cocaine]]]]
Probably a corruption of {{m|en|bundle}}; perhaps influenced by {{m|en|bindle}}.<ref name="OED2">“[http://dictionary.oed.com/cgi/entry/50022233 bindle²]” listed in the '''Oxford English Dictionary''' [2<sup>nd</sup> Ed.; 1989]</ref>

====Pronunciation====
* {{rhymes|ɪndəl|lang=en}}
* {{a|RP}} {{enPR|bĭnʹdl|bĭnʹdəl}}, {{IPA|/ˈbɪndl/|lang=en}},<ref name="OED2"/> {{IPAchar|/ˈbɪndəl/}},<ref name="OED2"/>

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|US|and|Canada|_|slang}} A [[bundle]] carried by a [[hobo]] (usually containing his possessions), often on a stick slung over the shoulder; a [[blanket roll]].<ref name="OED2"/>
#* '''2006''' {{w|Cormac McCarthy}}, ''{{w|The Road}}:''
#*: lastly he made a '''bindle''' in a plastic tarp of some cans of juice and cans of fruit and cans of vegetables…
# {{lb|en|US|and|Canada|_|slang}} Any bundle or [[package]]; specifically one containing [[narcotic]]s such as [[cocaine]], [[heroin]], or [[morphine]].<ref name="OED2"/>

